Finding: A cancelled required check strands the gate's exact veto revert.

Locations at M:
- warrant/gate.py:605-609: check_reasons maps an existing completed required check whose conclusion is cancelled to CHECK_RED.
- warrant/gate.py:1517-1523: approve_held consults ENDED_WITHOUT_CHECK and re-dispatches a revert's workflow only when CHECK_MISSING is present.
- warrant/gate.py:1570-1576: enforce_brakes treats the assessed exact revert as pending and opens no replacement, even while its check is red.
- tests/gate_test.py:1725-1745: E103 supplies CHECK_MISSING directly to its cancellation example, so it never tests the CHECK_RED result of an existing cancelled check.

Trigger and consequence:
The owner vetoes a braked constitutional change in time. The gate opens its exact revert. CI is cancelled after the required test check has been created; both that check and its workflow report completed/cancelled. The real assessment recognizes the exact revert and returns only CHECK_RED. approve_held returns no dispatch, and enforce_brakes returns no action because the exact revert is pending. Repeated identical reads cannot progress. The merged change remains despite the timely veto unless a person restarts CI. #558 handles cancellation before the required check exists, but its repair does not cover cancellation after that check exists. This leaves D's brake enforcement unfinished.

Observed in signed-store/Git fixtures at M (not an operation on GitHub):
- Required check absent, workflow cancelled: CHECK_MISSING; one ci.yml re-dispatch (control).
- Required check exists, completed/cancelled; workflow completed/cancelled: CHECK_RED; zero dispatches; no replacement revert (counterexample).
- Required check exists, completed/timed_out; workflow completed/timed_out: same fixture result.
- Required check and workflow successful: eligible; zero dispatches (control).
The cancellation counterexample alone supports the finding. The timed-out row is another supplied API-shaped fixture; no live GitHub timeout delivery was observed.

An isolated in-memory control widening only the CHECK_MISSING retry entry condition to CHECK_MISSING or CHECK_RED allows the existing ENDED_WITHOUT_CHECK filter to run and makes F1 pass. It preserves the successful control. This is causal evidence, not a reviewed or committed fix; a production repair needs its own ordinary PR, regression case and mutant.

